    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=5590": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Architectural Design",
      "description": "5590 Lecturer in Architectural Design - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept cookies Lecturer in Architectural Design School of Design & Creative Industries Location: Greenwich Campus Salary: £38,784 to £44,746\n            plus £4228 London weighting per annum Part Time Hours: 0.4FTE Contract Type: Fixed Term\n             - Maternity cover to June 2027 Release Date: Thursday 20 August 2026 Closing Date: Thursday 03 September 2026 Interview Date: Thursday 10 September 2026 Reference: 5590 On the 1 August 2026, the University of Greenwich and the University of Kent formed a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South-East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE but will work as part of the University of Greenwich academic division, contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity while also being part of a wider group that brings together the scale, resilience and shared ambition of both universities. Through LASE we aim to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. This is an exciting opportunity to become part of a collaborative architecture team committed to delivering innovative, research-informed teaching and an outstanding student experience. You will contribute to a holistic architectural curriculum that integrates design, technology, and histories and theories while responding to developments in architectural education and professional accreditation requirements. About the Role You will: Deliver engaging and inclusive architectural design teaching at undergraduate level, with a particular focus on first-year BA Architecture students. Support students through studio teaching, tutorials, assessment, and academic guidance. Collaborate with colleagues teaching architectural technology and histories and theories to deliver an integrated learning experience. Contribute to curriculum development and research-informed teaching activities. Participate in student recruitment, outreach, and external engagement activities. Contribute to the School's commitment to equality, diversity, inclusion, sustainability, and student success. The successful applicant must be available to work on Mondays and Thursdays and will be appointed on a fixed-term basis from September 2026 to June 2027. We particularly welcome applications from candidates who can bring creativity, inclusive teaching practice, and contemporary architectural expertise to our diverse student community. For an informal discussion about the post please contact Rahesh Ram on r.ram@gre.ac.uk Should you have any queries please contact the People Directorate Team on peopleoperationsdmin@gre.ac.uk Further details of the fantastic benefits and what we offer can be found here: Our benefits - what we offer | Jobs and careers | University of Greenwich and information on the university’s working principles: Working Principles and Guidelines | Documents | University of Greenwich To apply, please visit the University of Greenwich vacancies page and complete all details, including the supporting statements (please note attached CVs and personal statements will not be seen by the recruitment panel at the application stage): Current Vacancies - Jobs at Greenwich Employment Visa: Under the UK Government Points Based System scheme this role does not meet the criteria to be sponsored for a Skilled Worker Route application. We are looking for people who can help us deliver our mission of transforming lives through inspired teaching and research, through our values. Academic Career Pathways We are committed to building a strong, diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. We particularly encourage applications from [protected characteristic(s)], who are currently under-represented within the University of Greenwich at these levels/within these areas. We do this through taking positive action such as encouraging applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic, care leavers, disabled and LGBT+ people. As part of our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion, Time to Change Employer Pledge / Mentally Healthy Universities , we are committed to promoting and supporting the physical and mental health of all our staff, and removing barriers to improve inclusion. We encourage applicants to disclose experience of mental health problems so we can support them fully during our recruitment process and make any necessary reasonable adjustments. Any information disclosed will be kept confidential and separate from the job application form. We are making significant strides to understand and continuously improve our employees’ experience and we are committed to implementing progressive diversity talent management. Email details to a friend Apply online Further details: Job Description & Person Specification Share: View All Vacancies In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
    },
    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=5589": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Histories & Theories of Architecture",
      "description": "5589 Lecturer in Histories & Theories of Architecture - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept cookies Lecturer in Histories & Theories of Architecture School of Design & Creative Industries Location: Greenwich Campus Salary: £38,784 to £44,746\n            plus £4228 London weighting per annum Part Time Hours: 0.2FTE Contract Type: Fixed Term\n             - Maternity Cover to June 2027 Release Date: Thursday 20 August 2026 Closing Date: Thursday 03 September 2026 Interview Date: Thursday 10 September 2026 Reference: 5589 On the 1 August 2026, the University of Greenwich and the University of Kent formed a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South-East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE but will work as part of the University of Greenwich academic division, contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity while also being part of a wider group that brings together the scale, resilience and shared ambition of both universities. Through LASE we aim to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. The University of Greenwich is seeking an enthusiastic and committed Lecturer in Histories and Theories of Architecture (0.2 FTE) to join our Architecture team within the School of Design and Creative Industries. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator and researcher with expertise in architectural history, theory, and critical studies to contribute to our well-established Architecture programmes. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing and delivering engaging, research-informed teaching across our BA Architecture and Master of Architecture programmes. About the Role You will contribute to a vibrant academic environment by: Developing, delivering, and administering modules in Histories and Theories of Architecture. Teaching on undergraduate and postgraduate Architecture programmes. Designing innovative, research-informed learning experiences that support student success. Contributing to curriculum development and enhancement. Providing academic tutoring and pastoral support to students. Supporting recruitment, outreach, and engagement activities. Contributing to scholarly activity and the integration of research into teaching. Working collaboratively with colleagues across the Architecture portfolio and the wider School. The successful candidate must be available on Monday afternoons and Tuesday mornings . For an informal discussion about the post please contact Laura Bowie on l.bowie@gre.ac.uk Should you have any queries please contact the People Directorate Team on peopleoperationsdmin@gre.ac.uk Further details of the fantastic benefits and what we offer can be found here: Our benefits - what we offer | Jobs and careers | University of Greenwich and information on the university’s working principles: Working Principles and Guidelines | Documents | University of Greenwich To apply, please visit the University of Greenwich vacancies page and complete all details, including the supporting statements (please note attached CVs and personal statements will not be seen by the recruitment panel at the application stage): Current Vacancies - Jobs at Greenwich Employment Visa: Under the UK Government Points Based System scheme this role does not meet the criteria to be sponsored for a Skilled Worker Route application. We are looking for people who can help us deliver our mission of transforming lives through inspired teaching and research, through our values. Academic Career Pathways We are committed to building a strong, diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. We particularly encourage applications from [protected characteristic(s)], who are currently under-represented within the University of Greenwich at these levels/within these areas. We do this through taking positive action such as encouraging applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic, care leavers, disabled and LGBT+ people. As part of our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion, Time to Change Employer Pledge / Mentally Healthy Universities , we are committed to promoting and supporting the physical and mental health of all our staff, and removing barriers to improve inclusion. We encourage applicants to disclose experience of mental health problems so we can support them fully during our recruitment process and make any necessary reasonable adjustments. Any information disclosed will be kept confidential and separate from the job application form. We are making significant strides to understand and continuously improve our employees’ experience and we are committed to implementing progressive diversity talent management. Email details to a friend Apply online Further details: Job Description & Person Specification Share: View All Vacancies In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
    },
    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/vacancy.aspx?ref=5593": {
      "title": "Research Fellow",
      "description": "5593 Research Fellow - Virtual Production - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept cookies Research Fellow - Virtual Production School of Design & Creative Industries Location: Greenwich Campus Salary: £38,784 to £44,746\n            plus £4228 London weighting per annum Part Time Hours: to be discussed Contract Type: Fixed Term\n             - until 30th October 2026 Release Date: Wednesday 26 August 2026 Closing Date: Sunday 06 September 2026 Interview Date: To be confirmed Reference: 5593 On the 1 August 2026, the University of Greenwich and the University of Kent formed a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South-East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE but will work as part of the University of Greenwich academic division, contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity while also being part of a wider group that brings together the scale, resilience and shared ambition of both universities. Through LASE we aim to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. This opportunity is hosted and supported by the School of Design and Creative Industries in the Faculty of Law, Arts and Social Sciences. We are looking for a Research Fellow in virtual production to contribute to a research project within the Shared Hub for Immersive Future Technologies https://www.gre.ac.uk/las/ice/shift This is a short term fractional position over 9 weeks, during which you will contribute to the research project XR-Sync (Extended Reality Stage Synchronization), which aims to develop robust workflows to blend virtual sets with physical stages in real time. The project will: Synchronise VR headset views with the VP stage’s real-world tracking data. Deliver adaptable XR workflow solutions across a range of accessible systems, using diverse tracking systems, LED volumes and VR Headsets. Bring together academic (University of Greenwich) and industry expertise Leverage our AHRC funded facilities (Shared Hub for Immersive Future Technologies (SHIFT), University of Greenwich, By synchronizing the headset view with the stage’s real-world tracking data, users can step onto the stage and see the 3D environment precisely overlaid in their headset with accurate scale and alignment. This immediate, interactive visual feedback will enable creative teams to build, arrange, and refine set pieces and actor positions in real-time, reducing errors and guesswork in combining physical props with virtual sets. The outcomes of this work will enhance on-set efficiency, and enable real-time, on-stage exploration and decision-making for directors and crews working in Virtual Production filmmaking. The person appointed will be expected to: Support the Principal Investigator of XR-Sync in data analysis and in report and academic paper writing, in order to meet project aims and objectives and deliver required outputs. Support PI and other colleagues in the delivery of high quality, public facing research events, conferences or industry talks. Engage in research and enterprise and in so doing contribute to the research profile of the Shared Hub for Immersive Future Technologies and to the REF submission of the University of Greenwich. For an informal discussion about the post please contact Andrew Knight-Hill on A.Hill@gre.ac.uk Should you have any queries please contact the People Directorate Team on peopleoperationsdmin@gre.ac.uk Further details of the fantastic benefits and what we offer can be found here: Our benefits - what we offer | Jobs and careers | University of Greenwich and information on the university’s working principles: Working Principles and Guidelines | Documents | University of Greenwich To apply, please visit the University of Greenwich vacancies page and complete all details, including the supporting statements (please note attached CVs and personal statements will not be seen by the recruitment panel at the application stage): Current Vacancies - Jobs at Greenwich We are looking for people who can help us deliver our mission of transforming lives through inspired teaching and research, through our values. Academic Career Pathways We are committed to building a strong, diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. We particularly encourage applications from [protected characteristic(s)], who are currently under-represented within the University of Greenwich at these levels/within these areas. We do this through taking positive action such as encouraging applications from Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic, care leavers, disabled and LGBT+ people. As part of our commitment to Equality, Diversity and Inclusion, Time to Change Employer Pledge / Mentally Healthy Universities , we are committed to promoting and supporting the physical and mental health of all our staff, and removing barriers to improve inclusion. We encourage applicants to disclose experience of mental health problems so we can support them fully during our recruitment process and make any necessary reasonable adjustments. Any information disclosed will be kept confidential and separate from the job application form. We are making significant strides to understand and continuously improve our employees’ experience and we are committed to implementing progressive diversity talent management. Email details to a friend Apply online Further details: Job Description & Person Specification Share: View All Vacancies In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
    },
    "https://jobs.kent.ac.uk": {
      "title": "Your future starts here",
      "description": "Jobs at the University of Kent Skip to main content Home Current Vacancies Login Register About the University Working at Kent Kent & Medway Medical School Application Process Using AI in your application FAQ Contact Us Accessibility Statement Current LASE staff Contact Us Terms of Use Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n      We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n      To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Current Vacancies Login Register Menu Home Current Vacancies Login Register About the University Working at Kent Kent & Medway Medical School Guidance for Applicants Using AI in your application FAQ Contact Us Accessibility Statement Current LASE staff University of Kent Career Opportunities Jobs Your future starts here Your future starts here Welcome to the London and South East University Group, University of Kent academic division recruitment website where you will find details of our current employment opportunities. On the 1 August 2026, The University of Greenwich and the University of Kent formed a pioneering new multi-university group called London and South East (LASE) University Group. Should you join us, you will be employed by LASE and within this, you will be closely connected to and work across one of our academic divisions (University of Greenwich or University of Kent), contributing to its distinct strengths, community and identity. Combining these strengths, LASE brings scale, resilience and shared ambition to deliver outstanding education, impactful research, and meaningful regional and global impact. More information about the LASE University Group can be found here . We are proud to be one of the UK's leading universities. We were awarded silver in the government's Teaching Excellence Framework (TEF23) and the majority of our REF submissions were rated as world-leading or internationally excellent in the most recent Research Excellence Framework (REF) exercise. We have fantastic assets: our staff, our students, our campuses in Canterbury and Medway, and our proximity to London. So, whether you work in our research-led community of international academics or our team of talented professional services staff - Kent is a distinctive and attractive place to work. View the video below to get a feel for what working at Kent is like from existing staff. If you do not see a suitable opportunity at the moment, please visit our website regularly. Alternatively, to keep up to date with the opportunities we have available, please use our Jobs by Email service which will alert you to opportunities in the future. View our current vacancies Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register In This Section About the University Working at Kent Kent & Medway Medical School Guidance for Applicants Using AI in your application FAQ Contact Us Accessibility Statement Current LASE staff Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Advanced Job Search Quick Search Part of the London and South East University Group University of Kent, Canterbury, Kent, CT2 7NZ Connect with us on Facebook Follow us on X Follow us on Instagram Connect with us on LinkedIn Subscribe to us on Youtube Subscribe to us on TikTok tiktok-logo-4500 Affiliations About us About us About us Research Governance and planning Access agreements Transparency return Modern Slavery Act Statement Charity information Locations Support us What's on News Business services Career opportunities Sustainability Study Study Courses Undergraduates Postgraduates International students Part-time and short courses Student experience Accommodation Fees and funding Scholarships Term dates Information for Information for Applicants Parents and family Students Staff Alumni Business and partners Paying online © London and South East University Group Contact Us Terms of Use Cookies Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk": {
      "title": "Current vacancies",
      "description": "Current vacancies - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept cookies Current vacancies Our current vacancies are grouped together into staff categories or alternatively can be listed by campus. Select your preferred sort order to see the vacancies in which you are interested. Just click on the individual job links for further information about the post, the closing date and how to make an application. This is a fantastic time to join the University of Greenwich. We have an ambitious new strategy to be the best modern UK university by 2030. We are investing significantly in our student experience, our campuses, learning facilities and resources and as such our resources and staffing infra structure to support our growth in student numbers and our longer-term ambitions. The following vacancies are as a result of our recent growth and we welcome applications from those who share our aspirations and values of being inclusive, collaborative and impactful. Sort by: Category Faculty/Directorate Campus Filter Academic (3) Professional Services (8) Full list of current opportunities (11) If you can't find an opportunity at the moment use our email service to be alerted to opportunities in the future. As part of London and South East University Group (LASE) , you may also be interested in opportunities available at the University of Kent LASE University Group Staff Login If you are a current LASE University Group staff member and wish to search and apply for vacancies, including to internal only jobs , you must log in using your Greenwich / Kent username and password. If you register or log in with a personal email address, you will only be able to view vacancies open to external applicants. You can proceed to the login page - login In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Latest vacancies Doctoral Programme Manager Senior Student Retention & Success Officer Outreach and Student Recruitment Assistant View all vacancies Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
    },
    "https://jobs.gre.ac.uk/Subs/": {
      "title": "Job alerts",
      "description": "Job alerts - Jobs at Greenwich Skip to main content Jobs home Login Register Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Contact us Terms and conditions Cookies Accessibility Faculties Portal Jobs home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept cookies Job alerts We offer a free email service to alert you to jobs you may be interested in. This service will send you all the new vacancies in categories you may be interested in. You can refine your requirements with keywords and a desired salary range. You must Register or Login to use Job alerts. In this section Current vacancies Staff Visa Compliance Working at Greenwich Search jobs Equality, diversity and inclusion Sustainability Frequently asked questions Applying Find jobs Jobs by email Jobs by RSS Search jobs: Search Advanced job search Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten details Register Latest vacancies Doctoral Programme Manager Senior Student Retention & Success Officer Outreach and Student Recruitment Assistant View all vacancies Contact us | Terms and conditions | Cookies | Accessibility © University of Greenwich"
